# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Built skill package — distribute via a GitHub Release, not in source
*.skill.zip

# Local Meridian credentials / cached state (live in ~/.meridian, but guard anyway)
.meridian/
config.json
.ratelimit
fields.*.json

# Sensitive: generated risk-profile PDFs (contain personal data — never commit)
*.pdf
# The report verb's HTML fallback (no browser / conversion failed) and its print-to-PDF temp file
# carry the exact same personal data as the PDF, so they get the exact same rule. No exceptions
# needed: nothing HTML is committed.
*.html
# ...except these three, which are documentation and contain no stack data. Regenerate with
# `python scripts/make-guide.py` / `make-impact.py` / `make-brief.py`; keep them free of real names
# (use <person>). The brief and the guide ship to customers, so that rule is not optional there.
!Cyderes-Meridian-Skill-Guide.pdf
!Cyderes-Meridian-Skill-Enhancements.pdf
!Cyderes-MeridianCS-Brief.pdf

# Outputs a verb wrote into the skill folder: `> top.json`, `--format csv --out x.csv`. They carry
# the same personal data as the PDFs, and `git add -A` (the shipping flow) would commit them. Root
# and scripts/ only, because those are the two directories the commands run from; tracked JSON
# elsewhere (evals/, design/, references/) is unaffected. sbom.cdx.json is generated and tracked.
/*.json
!/sbom.cdx.json
/scripts/*.json
*.csv

# Local tool venv (see CLAUDE.md Testing). Not ignoring it would let a venv be committed,
# and make-package.py packages `git ls-files` -- it would ship inside a customer skill.
.venv*/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
